      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "1.1. Cross-Algorithm Interoperability & Invariant Verification"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999180400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Beyond isolated unit testing, StatCraft enforces mathematical and architectural invariants across all algorithm chains:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999181100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Mid-Rank & Tie Adjustment Invariant:**\n   * Canonical SPSS uses the fractional mid-rank assignment $(i + 1 + j) / 2.0$ for identical values across all procedures.\n   * Audited consistency across:\n     - [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/rank_cases.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/rank_cases.rs) (`TieHandling::Mean`)\n     - [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_twosample.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_twosample.rs) (`compute_ranks`)\n     - [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/kruskal_wallis.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/kruskal_wallis.rs) (`compute_joint_ranks`)\n     - [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs) (`wilcoxon_signed_rank_test`)\n     - [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/correlations.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/correlations.rs) (`spearman_rank_correlation`)\n   * Every procedure applies the identical tie variance correction factor $T = \\sum_{i=1}^m (t_i^3 - t_i)$."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999183800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Metadata Propagation & Measurement Level Chaining:**\n   * Transformation outputs generate canonical SPSS dictionary attributes:\n     - `BINNING` produces `Measure::Ordinal` with labeled bin ranges (`ValueLabels`).\n     - `RANK` produces `Measure::Ordinal` with standard naming prefixes (`R*`, `N*`, `P*`).\n     - `ADP` produces `Measure::Nominal` for partition variables (`_Partition_`) and `Measure::Scale` for continuous rescaled features (`*_transformed`).\n   * Chained downstream dialogs (`VariablePicker`, ANOVA, Crosstabs, T-Tests) recognize and respect these generated measurement levels without manual reconfiguration."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999185300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "3. **Row Filtering & Missing Value (SYSMIS) Isolation:**\n   * Universal filter support: analytical procedures evaluate `active_row_indices(ds)`, respecting user filters (`active_filter_var`).\n   * IEEE 754 `NaN` maps directly to SPSS System Missing (`SYSMIS`). All expressions and algorithmic procedures propagate `NaN` safely without panicking."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999186300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "4. **Global Weighting (`WEIGHT BY`) & File Split (`SPLIT FILE`):**\n   * Case weighting (`ds.row_weight`) is supported in moment calculations across:\n     - `crosstabs.rs`, `descriptives.rs`, `factor.rs`, `frequencies.rs`, `means.rs`, `regression.rs`, `reliability.rs`, `weight_cases.rs`.\n   * Status note: Weighting for bivariate correlations and t-tests, as well as automatic multi-group split-file table rendering in Output Viewer, are scheduled for future milestone updates."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999187700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
