      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "3. Detailed Verification Protocol"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999192000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 1: Descriptives, Frequencies, Crosstabs, and Means"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999192600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 1.1. `DESCRIPTIVES` (IBM Algorithms pp. 368–370)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/descriptives.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/descriptives.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `descriptives::tests::test_golden_oracle_descriptives_scipy`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Moments & Mean:** Spicer (1972) provisional means recurrence with case weights $W = \\sum w_i$:\n    $$\\bar{X} = \\frac{\\sum w_i X_i}{W}, \\quad s^2 = \\frac{1}{W-1} \\sum w_i (X_i - \\bar{X})^2, \\quad SE(\\bar{X}) = \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{W}}$$\n  * **Skewness:** Sample unbiased Fisher-Pearson skewness coefficient (Bliss, 1967):\n    $$g_1 = \\frac{W}{(W-1)(W-2)} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum w_i (X_i - \\bar{X})^3}{s^3}$$\n    Standard error: $SE(g_1) = \\sqrt{\\frac{6W(W-1)}{(W-2)(W+1)(W+3)}}$. Calculation is suppressed if $W \\le 2$ or $s^2 = 0$.\n  * **Kurtosis:** Bliss (1967) Fisher excess kurtosis:\n    $$g_2 = \\frac{W-1}{(W-2)(W-3)} \\left[ (W+1) \\frac{m_4}{m_2^2} - 3(W-1) \\right]$$\n    Standard error: $SE(g_2) = 2 \\cdot SE(g_1) \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{W^2 - 1}{(W-3)(W+5)}}$. Suppressed if $W \\le 3$ or $s^2 = 0$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999194300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 1.2. `FREQUENCIES` (IBM Algorithms pp. 446–448)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/frequencies.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/frequencies.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `frequencies::tests::test_frequency_numeric_sorting_and_quartiles`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * `Percent`: $\\frac{f_j}{W_{total}} \\times 100$ (including missing cases);\n  * `Valid Percent`: $\\frac{f_j}{W_{valid}} \\times 100$ (excluding missing cases);\n  * `Cumulative Percent`: Cumulative summation of `Valid Percent`;\n  * **Quantiles & Quartiles:** Canonical **SPSS HAVERAGE** linear interpolation (rank $r = p \\cdot (N + 1)$).\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999195600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 1.3. `CROSSTABS` (IBM Algorithms pp. 221–226)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/crosstabs.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/crosstabs.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `crosstabs_tests::tests::test_crosstabs_2x2_golden_oracle`, `crosstabs_tests::tests::test_fisher_exact_2x2_standard`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Expected counts: $E_{ij} = \\frac{R_i \\cdot C_j}{W}$, Raw residuals: $Res_{ij} = O_{ij} - E_{ij}$;\n  * Pearson's Chi-Square: $\\chi^2 = \\sum \\frac{(O_{ij} - E_{ij})^2}{E_{ij}}, \\quad df = (R-1)(C-1)$;\n  * Likelihood Ratio: $G^2 = 2 \\sum O_{ij} \\ln\\left(\\frac{O_{ij}}{E_{ij}}\\right)$ (terms with $O_{ij}=0$ evaluated strictly to 0);\n  * Yates Continuity Corrected ($2 \\times 2$):\n    $$\\chi^2_{Yates} = \\frac{W \\cdot \\left(\\max(0, |O_{11}O_{22} - O_{12}O_{21}| - 0.5 W)\\right)^2}{R_1 R_2 C_1 C_2}, \\quad df = 1$$\n  * Fisher's Exact Test: Two-sided $p$-value computed via log-gamma $\\ln \\Gamma(x)$ to prevent integer factorial overflow;\n  * Measures of Association: $\\Phi$ coefficient, Cramér's $V$, Pearson Contingency Coefficient.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999197400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 1.4. `MEANS` (IBM Algorithms pp. 662–665)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/means.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/means.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `means_tests::test_means_breakdown_golden_oracle`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * ANOVA variance decomposition:\n    $$SS_{Between} = \\sum W_j (\\bar{Y}_j - \\bar{Y})^2, \\; df = k - 1; \\quad SS_{Within} = \\sum (W_j - 1) s_j^2, \\; df = N - k$$\n    $$F = \\frac{MS_{Between}}{MS_{Within}}, \\quad p = I_{\\frac{df_2}{df_1 F + df_2}}\\left(\\frac{df_2}{2}, \\frac{df_1}{2}\\right)$$\n  * Measures of Association: $\\eta^2 = \\frac{SS_{Between}}{SS_{Total}}, \\quad \\eta = \\sqrt{\\eta^2}$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999199200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999199800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 2: Mean Comparisons (T-Tests & One-Way ANOVA)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999200300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 2.1. `ONE-SAMPLE T-TEST` (IBM Algorithms pp. 1061–1062)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_onesample.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_onesample.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `ttest_onesample::tests::test_golden_oracle_ttest_onesample_scipy`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  $$t = \\frac{\\bar{X} - \\text{TestValue}}{SE(\\bar{X})}, \\quad df = W - 1$$\n  $$p = I_{\\frac{df}{df + t^2}}\\left(\\frac{df}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$$\n  $$\\text{CI} = (\\bar{X} - \\text{TestValue}) \\pm t_{1 - \\alpha/2, df} \\cdot SE(\\bar{X})$$\n  Student's $t$ critical quantiles $t_{crit}$ computed via Acklam's rational approximation refined by Newton-Raphson root finding.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999201800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 2.2. `INDEPENDENT-SAMPLES T-TEST` (IBM Algorithms pp. 1058–1060)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_indep.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_indep.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `ttest_indep::tests::test_golden_oracle_against_scipy`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Levene's Test for Equality of Variances:** Canonical centering around group means:\n    $$Z_{kj} = |X_{kj} - \\bar{X}_k|, \\quad F = \\frac{MSB_Z}{MSW_Z}, \\quad df_1 = 1, \\; df_2 = n_1 + n_2 - 2$$\n  * **Equal Variances Assumed (Student's Pooled Variance):**\n    $$s_p^2 = \\frac{(n_1 - 1)s_1^2 + (n_2 - 1)s_2^2}{n_1 + n_2 - 2}, \\quad SE_{diff} = \\sqrt{s_p^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1} + \\frac{1}{n_2}\\right)}, \\quad df = n_1 + n_2 - 2$$\n  * **Equal Variances Not Assumed (Welch's Separate Variance with Satterthwaite df):**\n    $$SE_{welch} = \\sqrt{\\frac{s_1^2}{n_1} + \\frac{s_2^2}{n_2}}, \\quad df = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{s_1^2}{n_1} + \\frac{s_2^2}{n_2}\\right)^2}{\\frac{(s_1^2/n_1)^2}{n_1 - 1} + \\frac{(s_2^2/n_2)^2}{n_2 - 1}}$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999203300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 2.3. `PAIRED-SAMPLES T-TEST` (IBM Algorithms pp. 1060–1061)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_paired.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_paired.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `ttest_paired::tests::test_paired_ttest_golden_oracle`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Pearson correlation with two-tailed significance $t_r = r \\sqrt{\\frac{n-2}{1-r^2}}$;\n  * Paired Differences $D_i = X_i - Y_i$:\n    $$t = \\frac{\\bar{D}}{SE(\\bar{D})}, \\quad df = n - 1, \\quad \\text{CI} = \\bar{D} \\pm t_{crit} \\cdot SE(\\bar{D})$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999204700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 2.4. `ONE-WAY ANOVA` (IBM Algorithms pp. 802–806)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/anova_oneway.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/anova_oneway.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** ANOVA integration suite\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Sums of squares:\n    $$BSS = \\sum_{l=1}^k n_l (\\bar{X}_l - \\bar{X})^2, \\quad WSS = \\sum_{l=1}^k \\sum_{j=1}^{n_l} (X_{lj} - \\bar{X}_l)^2, \\quad TSS = BSS + WSS$$\n  * Fisher's $F$-test: $F = \\frac{BSS / (k-1)}{WSS / (N-k)}$, with $p$-value derived from regularized incomplete beta;\n  * Multi-group Levene Test ($k$ groups) with $df_1 = k-1, \\; df_2 = N-k$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999206700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
