    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 4: Nonparametric Tests"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999214800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 4.1. `MANN-WHITNEY U TEST` (IBM Algorithms pp. 796–797)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_twosample.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_twosample.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `nonparam_twosample_tests::test_mann_whitney_oracle_no_ties`, `test_mann_whitney_oracle_with_ties`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Combined cases ranked with fractional mid-ranks for ties. Group rank sums $S_1, S_2$.\n  * Mann-Whitney $U$ statistics:\n    $$U_1 = S_1 - \\frac{n_1(n_1+1)}{2}, \\quad U_2 = S_2 - \\frac{n_2(n_2+1)}{2}, \\quad U = \\min(U_1, U_2)$$\n  * Wilcoxon $W$: rank sum for the group with smaller mean rank.\n  * Expected value and tie-corrected variance:\n    $$\\mu_U = \\frac{n_1 n_2}{2}, \\quad \\sigma_U^2 = \\frac{n_1 n_2}{12} \\left( (N + 1) - \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^m (t_i^3 - t_i)}{N(N - 1)} \\right)$$\n  * Asymptotic standard normal test: $Z = \\frac{U - \\mu_U}{\\sigma_U}$, two-tailed $p$-value $p = 2(1 - \\Phi(|Z|))$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999216400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 4.2. `KRUSKAL-WALLIS ONE-WAY ANALYSIS OF VARIANCE` (IBM Algorithms pp. 800–801)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/kruskal_wallis.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/kruskal_wallis.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `kruskal_wallis_tests::test_kruskal_wallis_golden_oracle_distinct`, `test_kruskal_wallis_golden_oracle_ties`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Joint ranking of $N$ cases over $k$ groups with mid-ranks.\n  * Raw $H$ statistic:\n    $$H = \\frac{12}{N(N+1)} \\sum_{j=1}^k \\frac{R_j^2}{n_j} - 3(N+1)$$\n  * Tie correction factor and adjusted $H$:\n    $$H_{adj} = \\frac{H}{1 - \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^m (t_i^3 - t_i)}{N^3 - N}}$$\n  * Asymptotic significance: $\\chi^2$ survival function with $df = k - 1$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999218100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 4.3. `WILCOXON MATCHED-PAIRS SIGNED-RANK TEST` (IBM Algorithms p. 793)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `nonparam_related_tests::test_wilcoxon_signed_rank_oracle_with_ties`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Pairwise difference $D_i = Y_i - X_i$. Non-zero differences sorted by $|D_i|$ and ranked with mid-ranks.\n  * Positive sum $S_p = \\sum_{D_i > 0} R_i$, negative sum $S_n = \\sum_{D_i < 0} R_i$. Test statistic $W = \\min(S_p, S_n)$.\n  * Mean and tie-corrected variance:\n    $$\\mu_W = \\frac{n(n+1)}{4}, \\quad \\sigma_W^2 = \\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1) - 0.5 \\sum_{j=1}^l (t_j^3 - t_j)}{24}$$\n  * Continuity-corrected $Z$: $Z = \\frac{W - \\mu_W \\pm 0.5}{\\sigma_W}$, with asymptotic two-tailed $p$-value from standard normal.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999220000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 4.4. `SIGN TEST` (IBM Algorithms p. 792)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `nonparam_related_tests::test_sign_test_oracle`, `test_sign_test_equal_halves`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Difference counts: positive $n_+$, negative $n_-$, total valid non-zero pairs $n = n_+ + n_-$, $k = \\min(n_+, n_-)$.\n  * Exact two-tailed binomial probability via regularized incomplete beta function:\n    $$p = 2 \\sum_{i=0}^k \\binom{n}{i} 0.5^n = 2 \\cdot I_{0.5}(n - k, k + 1)$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999221500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
