    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 5: Data Transformations and Imputations"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999222600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 5.1. `RANK CASES` (IBM Algorithms pp. 904–906)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/rank_cases.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/rank_cases.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `rank_cases_tests::test_compute_ranks_no_ties`, `test_compute_ranks_with_ties`, `test_normal_scores`, `test_inv_normal_cdf_accuracy`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Ties methods: `MEAN` ($W_{i-1} + (w_i + 1)/2$), `LOW` ($W_{i-1} + 1$), `HIGH` ($W_i$), `SEQ` ($k+1$).\n  * Cumulative proportion estimators:\n    * **Blom (1958):** $F = \\frac{r - 3/8}{w + 1/4}$\n    * **Tukey (1962):** $F = \\frac{r - 1/3}{w + 1/3}$\n    * **Rankit:** $F = \\frac{r - 1/2}{w}$\n    * **Van der Waerden:** $F = \\frac{r}{w + 1}$\n  * **Normal Scores:** $Z = \\Phi^{-1}(F)$ computed using Peter J. Acklam's rational approximation ($\\le 1.15 \\times 10^{-9}$ error).\n  * Fractional ranks ($r / w$), Percent ($100 r / w$), and Ntiles ($\\lceil \\frac{r k}{w} \\rceil$).\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999224000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 5.2. `REPLACE MISSING VALUES` (IBM Algorithms pp. 66, 117, 143, 960)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/replace_missing.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/replace_missing.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `replace_missing::tests::test_linear_interpolation`, `test_linear_trend`, `test_mean_nearby_imputation`, `test_median_nearby_imputation`, `test_series_mean_imputation`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Linear Interpolation:** $y_i = y_0 + \\frac{i - i_0}{i_1 - i_0}(y_1 - y_0)$ between surrounding valid cases.\n  * **Series Mean:** $\\bar{y} = \\frac{1}{n_{valid}} \\sum y_i$.\n  * **Mean & Median of Nearby Points:** Symmetric span window $j \\in [\\max(0, i - span), \\min(n - 1, i + span)], j \\ne i$.\n  * **Linear Trend at Point:** Bivariate linear regression $y = a + b \\cdot t$ where $t$ is case sequence index.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999225500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 5.3. `OPTIMAL BINNING` (IBM Algorithms pp. 130, 816–826)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/optimal_binning.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/optimal_binning.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `optimal_binning::tests::test_perfect_two_class_split`, `test_null_handling`, `test_constant_feature`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Supervised discretization based on Fayyad & Irani (1993) Minimum Description Length Principle (MDLP) and Shannon entropy:\n    $$Ent(S) = - \\sum_{i=1}^k p_i \\log_2 p_i$$\n    $$Gain(S, T) = Ent(S) - \\frac{|S_1|}{|S|} Ent(S_1) - \\frac{|S_2|}{|S|} Ent(S_2)$$\n    $$MDLP \\; Stopping: Gain(S, T) > \\frac{\\log_2(N - 1)}{N} + \\frac{\\Delta(S, T)}{N}$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999226700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
