    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 6: Automated Data Preparation (ADP) (IBM Algorithms pp. 63–80)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999227700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 6.1. Target & Predictor Screening (IBM Algorithms pp. 66–67)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/screening.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/screening.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `adp::tests::test_screening_removes_constant_and_high_missing`\n* **Mathematical Invariants:**\n  * Maximum missing rate threshold $th_{missing} \\in (0, 1)$ (default $0.5$): excludes predictors if $\\frac{n_{missing}}{N} > th_{missing}$.\n  * Single category predominance threshold $th_{freq} \\in (0, 1)$ (default $0.95$): excludes categorical predictors if $\\max_k \\frac{count_k}{N_{valid}} > th_{freq}$.\n  * Minimum category diversity: categorical predictors with single distinct valid value are excluded (zero variance).\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999228900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 6.2. Outlier Detection & Winsorization / Trimming (IBM Algorithms pp. 68–70)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/outliers.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/outliers.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `adp::tests::test_outlier_handling_winsorize_and_trim`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Standard Deviation Cutoff:** Mean $\\bar{X}$ and sample standard deviation $s$ with multiplier $k$ (default $k = 3.0$):\n    $$Bound_{lower} = \\bar{X} - k \\cdot s, \\quad Bound_{upper} = \\bar{X} + k \\cdot s$$\n  * **Interquartile Range (IQR / Tukey) Cutoff:** Empirical percentiles $Q_1 = P_{25}$, $Q_3 = P_{75}$, $IQR = Q_3 - Q_1$:\n    $$Bound_{lower} = Q_1 - k \\cdot IQR, \\quad Bound_{upper} = Q_3 + k \\cdot IQR \\quad (k = 1.5 \\text{ or } 3.0)$$\n  * **Winsorization:** Clamps values exceeding bounds:\n    $$X'_i = \\min(\\max(X_i, Bound_{lower}), Bound_{upper})$$\n  * **Trimming:** Sets values outside $[Bound_{lower}, Bound_{upper}]$ to System-Missing (`NaN`).\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999230900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 6.3. Continuous Predictor Transformation & Rescaling (IBM Algorithms pp. 71–74)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/transform.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/transform.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `adp::tests::test_zscore_and_minmax_transforms`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Z-Score Standardization:** $Z_i = \\frac{X_i - \\bar{X}}{s}$.\n  * **Min-Max Rescaling to $[a, b]$:**\n    $$X'_i = a + (b - a) \\cdot \\frac{X_i - X_{min}}{X_{max} - X_{min}}$$\n  * **Box-Cox Power Transformation:** Parameter grid search over $\\lambda \\in [-2.0, 2.0]$ maximizing profile log-likelihood:\n    $$y_i^{(\\lambda)} = \\begin{cases} \\frac{y_i^\\lambda - 1}{\\lambda \\cdot \\dot{y}^{\\lambda - 1}}, & \\lambda \\ne 0 \\\\ \\dot{y} \\ln(y_i), & \\lambda = 0 \\end{cases}$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999232400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 6.4. Partitioning & Data Split (IBM Algorithms p. 64)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/partition.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/partition.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `adp::tests::test_dataset_partition_ratios`\n* **Mathematical Invariants:**\n  * Deterministic stratified and random sampling into Training ($p_{train}$), Testing ($p_{test}$), and Validation ($p_{holdout}$) subsets.\n  * Encoded into nominal partition variable `_Partition_` ($1 = \\text{Train}, 2 = \\text{Test}, 3 = \\text{Holdout}$) preserving class priors across strata.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999233800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 6.5. Feature Selection & Predictive Power (IBM Algorithms pp. 75–80)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/predictive_power.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/predictive_power.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `adp::tests::test_predictive_power_ranking`\n* **Mathematical Invariants:**\n  * Continuous-Target: Pearson correlation $r^2$ or ANOVA $F$-statistic / $\\eta^2 = \\frac{SS_{between}}{SS_{total}}$.\n  * Categorical-Target: Cramér's $V = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\chi^2}{N \\min(r-1, c-1)}}$ or information gain ratio based on Shannon entropy.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999234900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 7: Mathematical Expressions & Evaluator (`COMPUTE`)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999235400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 7.1. Expression Syntax, Shunting-Yard AST & Operator Precedence\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/expr_eval/`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/expr_eval/) (`lexer.rs`, `parser.rs`, `eval.rs`, `mod.rs`), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/compute_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/compute_cmd.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `expr_eval::tests::test_arithmetic_precedence`, `expr_eval::tests::test_relational_and_logical_operators`, `commands::compute_cmd::tests::test_compute_sps_syntax`, `commands::compute_cmd::tests::test_compute_new_variable_and_undo`\n* **Mathematical & Algorithmic Invariants:**\n  * **Parser Architecture:** Dijkstra's Shunting-yard algorithm translating infix syntax to Reverse Polish Notation (RPN) stack nodes.\n  * **Current Precedence Hierarchy in `parser.rs`:**\n    1. Unary `+`, `-`, and Logical `NOT` / `~` (precedence 7);\n    2. Exponentiation `**`, `^` (precedence 6, right-associative);\n    3. Multiplicative `*`, `/` (precedence 5);\n    4. Additive `+`, `-` (precedence 4);\n    5. Relational operators: `=`, `<>` / `~=` / `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` (precedence 3);\n    6. Logical conjunction `AND` / `&` (precedence 2);\n    7. Logical disjunction `OR` / `|` (precedence 1).\n* **Audit Finding [DIVERGENCE]:**\n  1. In canonical IBM SPSS (Syntax Reference, *Order of Operations*), exponentiation `**` has higher precedence than unary `-`/`+`. Under SPSS canon, `-2**2` evaluates to `-(2**2) = -4`. In current `parser.rs`, unary minus at precedence 7 precedes `**` at 6, yielding `(-2)**2 = +4`.\n  2. In canonical IBM SPSS, `NOT` is evaluated *after* relational operators. In SPSS, `NOT a = b` evaluates as `NOT (a = b)`. In current `parser.rs`, `NOT` at precedence 7 precedes relational operators (precedence 3), parsing as `(NOT a) = b` unless explicit parentheses are supplied."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999237400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 7.2. Canonical Math & Statistical Aggregate Functions\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/expr_eval/eval.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/expr_eval/eval.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `expr_eval::tests::test_math_functions`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Elementary Transformations:**\n    $$\\text{SQRT}(x) = \\begin{cases} \\sqrt{x}, & x \\ge 0 \\\\ \\text{SYSMIS}, & x < 0 \\end{cases}, \\quad \\text{EXP}(x) = e^x, \\quad \\text{LN}(x) = \\begin{cases} \\ln(x), & x > 0 \\\\ \\text{SYSMIS}, & x \\le 0 \\end{cases}$$\n    $$\\text{LOG10}(x) = \\begin{cases} \\log_{10}(x), & x > 0 \\\\ \\text{SYSMIS}, & x \\le 0 \\end{cases}, \\quad \\text{ABS}(x) = |x|, \\quad \\text{RND}(x) = \\lfloor x + 0.5 \\rfloor, \\quad \\text{TRUNC}(x) = \\text{sign}(x) \\lfloor |x| \\rfloor$$\n  * **Statistical Aggregates Across Variables:**\n    $$\\text{SUM}(x_1, \\dots, x_k) = \\sum_{x_i \\in \\text{valid}} x_i, \\quad \\text{MEAN}(x_1, \\dots, x_k) = \\frac{1}{|\\text{valid}|} \\sum_{x_i \\in \\text{valid}} x_i$$\n    $$\\text{MIN}(x_1, \\dots, x_k) = \\min_{x_i \\in \\text{valid}} x_i, \\quad \\text{MAX}(x_1, \\dots, x_k) = \\max_{x_i \\in \\text{valid}} x_i$$\n* **Audit Finding [DIVERGENCE]:**\n  1. Missing standard SPSS mathematical functions: `SIN`, `COS`, `TAN`, `MOD`, as well as canonical SPSS alias `LG10` (currently only `LOG10` is recognized).\n  2. In canonical IBM SPSS, `MEAN(x1, x2)` requires *all* arguments to be non-missing unless `.n` suffix is specified (`MEAN.1`). In current `eval.rs`, `MEAN` evaluates if at least one argument is valid."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999239200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 7.3. 3-Valued Logic & Missing Value Propagation (Never Crash)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/expr_eval/mod.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/expr_eval/mod.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `expr_eval::tests::test_nan_safety`, `expr_eval::tests::test_variables_and_row_eval`\n* **Mathematical Invariants:**\n  * Strict missing value contagion: arithmetic operations with `NaN` produce `NaN` (`SYSMIS`).\n  * Division by zero: safely evaluates to `NaN` without panic.\n* **Audit Finding [DIVERGENCE]:**\n  * Canonical SPSS 3-valued logic (Kleene 3VL) dictates that `TRUE OR MISSING` evaluates to `TRUE` (1.0) and `FALSE AND MISSING` evaluates to `FALSE` (0.0). In `mod.rs` (lines 74–77), blanket missing-check `if a.is_nan() || b.is_nan() { stack.push(f64::NAN); continue; }` unconditionally produces `NaN` for all binary operators, deviating from Kleene logic for short-circuiting Boolean combinations."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999240800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
