    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 8: Time Series Transformations & Case Shifts"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413999241800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 8.1. Difference & Seasonal Difference Operators (`DIFF`, `SDIFF`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/time_series.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/time_series.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/time_series_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/time_series_cmd.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `time_series::tests::test_diff_order_1`, `time_series::tests::test_diff_order_2`, `time_series::tests::test_diff_with_missing`, `time_series::tests::test_seasonal_diff`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Non-Seasonal Difference of Order $d$ (`DIFF`):**\n    $$\\Delta^1 X_t = X_t - X_{t-1}, \\quad \\Delta^d X_t = \\Delta^{d-1} X_t - \\Delta^{d-1} X_{t-1} \\quad (d \\ge 1)$$\n    For $t \\le d$, $\\Delta^d X_t = \\text{SYSMIS}$. If $X_t$ or any required antecedent is missing, $\\Delta^d X_t = \\text{SYSMIS}$.\n  * **Seasonal Difference of Period $s$ (`SDIFF`):**\n    $$\\Delta_s X_t = X_t - X_{t-s} \\quad (s \\ge 1)$$\n    For $t \\le s$, $\\Delta_s X_t = \\text{SYSMIS}$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999243200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 8.2. Moving Averages & Cumulative Sums (`SMA`, `CSUM`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/time_series.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/time_series.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `time_series::tests::test_sma`, `time_series::tests::test_sma_with_missing`, `time_series::tests::test_csum`, `time_series::tests::test_csum_with_missing`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Trailing Simple Moving Average (`SMA(k)`):**\n    $$SMA_k(X_t) = \\frac{1}{k} \\sum_{i=0}^{k-1} X_{t-i} \\quad (k \\ge 1)$$\n    For $t < k$, $SMA_k(X_t) = \\text{SYSMIS}$. If any value in the trailing window $[t-k+1, t]$ is missing, the average evaluates to `SYSMIS`.\n  * **Cumulative Sum (`CSUM`):**\n    $$CSUM(X_t) = \\sum_{i=1}^t X_i$$\n    Strict missing value cascade: if $X_m = \\text{SYSMIS}$, then $CSUM(X_t) = \\text{SYSMIS}$ for all $t \\ge m$.\n* **Audit Finding [DISCREPANCY]:**\n  * In canonical IBM SPSS (`CREATE` command pp. 220–225), `SMA(span)` calculates a **centered** moving average: if `span` is odd, the window is centered on the current term $(t - \\lfloor k/2 \\rfloor \\dots t + \\lfloor k/2 \\rfloor)$; if even, it centers between terms.\n  * In `time_series.rs` (lines 88–122), `SimpleMovingAverage(span)` computes a **trailing / prior** window $[t - span + 1 \\dots t]$. In IBM SPSS, this exact trailing transformation is known as **`PMA(span)` (Prior Moving Average)**, not `SMA`.\n  * `CSUM` exactly reproduces the canonical SPSS algorithm including `SYSMIS` cascade."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999245100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 8.3. Shift Operators (`LAG`, `LEAD`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/shift.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/shift.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/shift_values_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/shift_values_cmd.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `shift::tests::test_compute_shift_lag`, `shift::tests::test_compute_shift_lead`, `shift::tests::test_compute_shift_zero_step`, `commands::shift_values_cmd::tests::test_shift_values_to_sps`\n* **Mathematical Invariants:**\n  * **Lag Operator:** $LAG_k(X)_t = X_{t-k}$ for $t > k$; $LAG_k(X)_t = \\text{SYSMIS}$ for $t \\le k$.\n  * **Lead Operator:** $LEAD_k(X)_t = X_{t+k}$ for $t \\le N - k$; $LEAD_k(X)_t = \\text{SYSMIS}$ for $t > N - k$.\n  * Preserves underlying data types across numbers, strings, and missing values.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413999246500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
